        "type": "text",
        "text": "[gbrain notice degraded_recall kind=degraded]\nwhy: Recall was degraded (keyword_only_no_embedding_provider): semantic (vector) search did not run, so matches phrased differently from the query can be missing. Treat a thin or empty result as \"not found with a degraded search\", never as \"the brain has nothing on this\". This brain was set up keyword-only by the user's choice; mention it only if the user asks why something was not found. No query text was sent to an embedding provider. If the user wants semantic search, `gbrain doctor --json` names the enable command; turning it on needs their consent."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "[gbrain notice recall_hint kind=info]\nwhy: The facts in this response are the newest saved facts: `query` searches pages and does not rank facts. `question` ranks saved facts by relevance to a question (it does not search pages).\nfix: recall {\"query\":\"Grostaitheim sister's cat\",\"question\":\"Grostaitheim sister's cat\"}\nnext: run"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "[gbrain degraded: embed_unavailable] This result is partial or degraded: never report \"no notes\" or \"not found\" from it."
      }
    ],
    "details": {
      "mcpServer": "gbrain",
      "mcpTool": "recall"
    }
  }
}
